{
  "_comment": "Language-neutral contract cases for the model registry (TEAM-4990 / TEAM-4997). src/lib/models-registry.test.ts iterates every case; the Python/Lambda twin imports this same file, so DO NOT change a case's name, input or expected value without updating both sides. `registry` is \"seed\" (src/config/models.json as shipped) or null (no registry available at all); `patch` mutates the seed with explicit typed ops (merge into defaults/tiers/agents/legacyAliases, replace quarantine, append addRows, delete named fields via dropRowFields) rather than dotted paths, because model ids contain dots and a dotted path would be ambiguous. DEVIATIONS from the design table, both deliberate: (1) the four global.anthropic.* ids are CATALOG ROWS, not aliases of the us.* rows - their published rates genuinely differ - so the design's `alias-global` case is `raw-id-global` here and resolves to ITSELF with source \"catalog\"; (2) the two dated-duplicate cases patch the seed (whose sonnet-5 row is already the base id) instead of carrying a hand-written inline document, so the base/dated pair under test is the real one. `source` is a CLOSED enum: \"override\" | \"agents\" | \"defaults\" | \"env\" | \"literal\" are chain steps, emitted only by resolveAgentModel/resolveCodingModel; \"tier\" | \"legacyAlias\" | \"catalog\" | \"passthrough\" are lookup kinds, emitted by resolveModel and carried as `via` on a chain result. An alias hit reports \"catalog\" - the row was found, and how is not the caller's business. There is no \"alias\", \"legacy\", \"agent\", \"default\" or \"quarantine_fallback\". For `validate` cases, `expected.readable` is the READ-time verdict (would a loader serve this document?), which tolerates NON_FATAL_READ_REASONS (`unknown_agent`, `unprobed`); when absent it defaults to `expected.ok`, so a document with only fatal errors is unreadable and a clean one is readable.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "tier-claude",
      "note": "Driven through the pure resolver, not the agent chain: a bare tier word is a legal resolveModel input.",
      "registry": "seed",
      "input": { "kind": "resolveModel", "value": "opus", "cli": "claude" },
      "expected": { "modelId": "us.anthropic.claude-opus-5", "source": "tier" }
    },
    {
      "name": "tier-codex",
      "registry": "seed",
      "input": { "kind": "resolveModel", "value": "sol", "cli": "codex" },
      "expected": { "modelId": "us.openai.gpt-6-sol", "source": "tier" }
    },
    {
      "name": "raw-id",
      "registry": "seed",
      "input": { "kind": "resolveModel", "value": "us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5" },
      "expected": { "modelId": "us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5", "source": "catalog" }
    },
    {
      "name": "alias-bare",
      "registry": "seed",
      "input": { "kind": "resolveModel", "value": "claude-opus-5-5" },
      "expected": { "modelId": "us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5", "source": "catalog" }
    },
    {
      "name": "raw-id-global",
      "note": "global.* is its own row at its own rate, so it resolves to itself - it is not an alias of us.*.",
      "registry": "seed",
      "input": { "kind": "resolveModel", "value": "global.anthropic.claude-opus-5" },
      "expected": { "modelId": "global.anthropic.claude-opus-5", "source": "catalog" }
    },
    {
      "name": "legacy-alias",
      "registry": "seed",
      "input": { "kind": "resolveModel", "value": "claude-sonnet-45" },
      "expected": { "modelId": "us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5", "source": "legacyAlias" }
    },
    {
      "name": "quarantined-id",
      "note": "The override is REJECTED, not silently honoured: resolveModel returns null and the chain drops to defaults, keeping the rejection in diagnostics.",
      "registry": "seed",
      "patch": { "quarantine": ["us.anthropic.claude-opus-5"] },
      "input": {
        "kind": "resolveAgentModel",
        "agentId": "agentcore_hub_backend_dev",
        "override": "us.anthropic.claude-opus-5"
      },
      "expected": {
        "modelId": "us.anthropic.claude-fable-5-1",
        "source": "defaults",
        "via": "catalog",
        "diagnostics": [{ "step": "override", "reason": "quarantined" }]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "unknown-raw",
      "note": "A vendor-qualified id the catalog has never seen is passed through, not rejected - discovery lags reality.",
      "registry": "seed",
      "input": { "kind": "resolveModel", "value": "vendor.model-x" },
      "expected": { "modelId": "vendor.model-x", "source": "passthrough" }
    },
    {
